Description: core: One conversion table per pair of colour descriptions, built once and reused
 .
 ColorConversionTable::get() builds, from ColorPipeline::create and the colour
 description's own matrices, everything the conversion of a pair of descriptions
 needs (the pipeline, the shader's uniforms), caches it (a handful of tables, least
 recently used out) and returns the same table for as long as neither description
 changes. GLShader::setColorspaceUniforms() now takes its values from the table, so
 the scene pass and every other user convert with the same numbers and the matrices
 are not computed for each draw.
 .
 forCopy() decides once per pair whether the composed eyes of one output can be
 converted into the colour space of another one and give what painting the scene
 again would give (within one level of 10 bits, for SDR content, and for HDR content
 when some is on screen); the same table converts HDR content (PQ) into an SDR
 output with deep colour, in floating point until it is encoded once at the output's
 depth. testColorConversion: built once and reused, the copy equals painting again
 per channel at 8, 10 and 12 bits, a PQ ramp onto 10, 12 and 16 bit SDR keeps its
 steps (4095 of 4096 codes at 12 bits, no jump above one level), HDR content leaves
 the copy on the old path with the reason.
